Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:34:57 +0100
Subject: [M156] [builtins] Track Promise.any reject closure state in the
 errors array

Original change's description:
> [builtins] Track Promise.any reject closure state in the errors array
>
> PromiseAnyRejectElementClosure previously recorded its one-shot
> `[[AlreadyCalled]]` state by overwriting `target.context` with the
> native context and checking `IsNativeContext(context)` against the
> incoming context register. Because Maglev and TurboFan treat
> JSFunction::context as immutable and constant-fold it for known call
> targets, an optimized caller could invoke the same reject closure
> repeatedly with its original PromiseAnyRejectElementContext, driving
> remainingElementsCount to zero while unfilled PromiseHole elements
> remained in `AggregateError.errors`.
>
> Check `remainingElementsCount == 0` and
> `errors.objects[index] != PromiseHole` in PromiseAnyRejectElementClosure
> instead of mutating `target.context`, and check that the rejected value
> is not PromiseHole, matching PromiseAllResolveElementClosure
> (https://crrev.com/c/5000306).
>
